From ece91da75b62889b35c3cae3f98a1ea259dc83f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:54:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(tasks): keep the newest edit when task saves answer
 out of order

Two quick edits in the task detail (the due date, then the priority) send two
PATCH requests that overlap. Each response was applied as it arrived, so when
the first one landed last the detail and every cached copy fell back to the
older value, and the next save sent that older value back to the server.

Only the newest save of a task now writes its response; it carries every
edit made before it.
